message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the paper below."
title: "TBMD: Tensor-Based Modal Decomposition Method"
type: software
version: 2.2.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/denis-samatov/tensor-based-modal-decomposition-method"
# Prepared version: no release date or DOI is asserted before archival publication.
abstract: >-
  Python research library and Brugge benchmark for tensor-based modal decomposition,
  sparse sensing and field reconstruction. Version 2.2.0 includes nested optimization,
  matched independent-3D/joint-4D E9 comparisons, frozen selections, stored derived results,
  environment lock, claim checks and generators for the current manuscript.
  Restricted simulation inputs are not included. The earlier v2.1.0 DOI does not identify
  this revision.
keywords:
  - reservoir monitoring
  - sensor placement
  - proper orthogonal decomposition
  - Tucker decomposition
  - compressive sensing
